Fixed. `Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift:4`.

**Bug:** the old code split on spaces and kept tokens starting with `#`. That missed any tag not surrounded by spaces — `#urgent` glued to a comma (`shopping list,#urgent.`) and `(#ideas)` buried in parens.

**Fix:** replaced the split/filter with an `NSRegularExpression` scan for `#[\p{L}\p{N}_]+` anywhere in the string. It:
- picks up `#urgent` after the comma and `(#ideas)` inside parentheses (both now work),
- preserves appearance order (matches are returned left-to-right),
- keeps all existing behavior: `hello #world #swift` → `["world","swift"]`, and no-tag text → `[]`.

Verified by compiling and running the function standalone against `shopping list,#urgent.` → `["urgent"]`, `(#ideas)` → `["ideas"]`, plus the two existing test cases. Full `swift build`/`swift test` couldn't run — the sandbox blocks `swift` here (`sandbox_apply: Operation not permitted`), so I validated the logic with `swiftc` directly.


